  "title": "Claude Code 2.0 Agentic Coding: No, other agents aren't even close.",
  "description": "Codex CLI and Gemini CLI are NOWHERE NEAR Claude Code 2.0 and it's not even close.\n\nClaude 4.5 Sonnet speaks for itself. But when you put Claude 4.5 Sonnet in Claude Code 2.0 you get the best agentic coding tool by far bar none.\n\n🎥 Featured Links:\n\n- TACTICAL AGENTIC CODING: https://agenticengineer.com/tactical-agentic-coding?y=nGhsgdQplHw\n\n- CLAUDE 4.5 SONNET RELEASE POST: https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-sonnet-4-5\n\n- CLAUDE CODE 2.0 RELEASE POST: https://www.anthropic.com/news/enabling-claude-code-to-work-more-autonomously\n\n- CLAUDE AGENT SDK: https://docs.claude.com/en/api/agent-sdk/python\n\n- OUTPUT STYLE GIST: https://gist.github.com/disler/c7719b79a10762d87e89617c1f4a11c1\n\n🚀 In this agentic coding devlog, IndyDevDan demonstrates the true power of Claude Code 2.0 and Claude 4.5 Sonnet. Watch as we migrate from the old Claude Code SDK to the new Claude Agent SDK using tactical agentic coding principles. This isn't just another coding tutorial - this is a masterclass in scaling compute with AI agents.\n\n🛠️ Witness firsthand how we compose agentic prompts, chain custom slash commands, and deploy fleets of AI agents across dedicated agent devices. We're not just talking theory - we're showing you exactly how to build systems that build themselves. From scout-plan-build workflows to out-of-loop agent systems, this video reveals the tactics that separate amateur prompt engineers from true agentic engineers.\n\n💡 Key highlights include:\n- Scout-Plan-Build workflow with multiple parallel agents\n- Custom slash commands that compose and chain together\n- Dedicated agent devices running autonomous workflows\n- Context engineering with the R&D framework (Reduce and Delegate)\n- Real-time migration of 8 custom agents to the new Claude Agent SDK\n- Building OpenAI Agent SDK prototypes with web search and function tools\n\n🔥 The big idea: Stop prompting back and forth with single agents. Start building the system that builds the system. Your engineering output will be absolutely transformative once you master these tactical agentic coding patterns.\n\n🌟 Whether you're drowning in manual coding or ready to 10x your engineering output, this video shows you exactly how IndyDevDan uses Claude Code 2.0 and tactical agentic prompts to accomplish complex migrations and prototype builds with just TWO prompts.\n\nDon't get left behind. The context window is your limit, but with proper context engineering and agentic prompts, you can scale far beyond traditional AI coding.\n\n#claudecode #agenticcoding #promptengineering",
